   Token-driven via the --arxiv-{success,info,warning,error}-* families
   (see color-mapping.md "Status & alert colors — shared"). Structurally
   identical to the internal stylesheet's .ds-alert; only the token names
   differ (--arxiv- prefix here).

   Color is never the sole signal — pair each variant with a distinct icon
   shape AND a leading word (WCAG 1.4.1). ARIA: role="status" for
   success/info (polite), role="alert" for warning/error (assertive);
   icons carry aria-hidden="true". Inline links inherit the variant color
   and stay underlined, per the link policy.

   Promoted from arxiv-mockups/design-patterns/alert-styles.html (2026-05-28).

   Example:
     <div class="ds-alert ds-alert-info" role="status">
       <svg class="ds-alert-icon" aria-hidden="true">…</svg>
       <div class="ds-alert-content">
         <p class="ds-alert-title">Viewing an older version</p>
         <p>A newer version of this paper exists — <a href="...">see v3</a>.</p>
       </div>
     </div>
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.ds-alert {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 11px;
  padding: 12px 14px;
  border: 1px solid;
  border-left-width: 4px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-family: var(--arxiv-font-sans);
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
.ds-alert-icon {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  margin-top: 1px;
  stroke: currentColor;
  fill: none;
}
.ds-alert-content { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
.ds-alert-title { font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 2px; }
.ds-alert-content p { margin: 0; }
.ds-alert a {
  color: inherit;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 2px;
}
.ds-alert-dismiss {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-top: -2px;
  background: none;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: inherit;
  opacity: 0.7;
  padding: 2px;
  border-radius: 3px;
  line-height: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
}
.ds-alert-dismiss:hover { opacity: 1; }
.ds-alert-dismiss:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--arxiv-focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }
.ds-alert-dismiss svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; stroke: currentColor; fill: none; }

/* Variants — bg + border + fg (icon uses currentColor = fg) */
.ds-alert-success { background: var(--arxiv-success-bg); border-color: var(--arxiv-success-border); color: var(--arxiv-success-fg); }
.ds-alert-info    { background: var(--arxiv-info-bg);    border-color: var(--arxiv-info-border);    color: var(--arxiv-info-fg); }
.ds-alert-warning { background: var(--arxiv-warning-bg); border-color: var(--arxiv-warning-border); color: var(--arxiv-warning-fg); }
.ds-alert-error   { background: var(--arxiv-error-bg);   border-color: var(--arxiv-error-border);   color: var(--arxiv-error-fg); }

/* Dark mode — overrides the status tokens only. This is the first
   dark-aware block in the public stylesheet; broader public dark mode is
   still pending (color-mapping.md open question). Guarded by data-theme
   so a page can lock to light with <html data-theme="light">. */
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --arxiv-link-blue:       #64b5f6;  /* 7.84:1 on Repository Brown ✓ AAA */
    --arxiv-link-hover:      #90caf9;
    --arxiv-link-visited:    #c084e0;  /* 6.30:1 on Repository Brown ✓ AA */
    --arxiv-success-bg:      #1e2b0d;
    --arxiv-success-border:  #8fbd3a;
    --arxiv-success-fg:      #c5e1a5;  /* 10.4:1 ✓ AAA */
    --arxiv-info-bg:         #132433;
    --arxiv-info-border:     #64b5f6;
    --arxiv-info-fg:         #90caf9;  /* 9.0:1 ✓ AAA */
    --arxiv-warning-bg:      #2e2410;
    --arxiv-warning-border:  #e8b800;
    --arxiv-warning-fg:      #ffe082;  /* 11.8:1 ✓ AAA */
    --arxiv-error-bg:        #2d1414;
    --arxiv-error-border:    #e57373;
    --arxiv-error-fg:        #ef9a9a;  /* 8.0:1 ✓ AAA */
  }
}

/* OS accessibility signals. forced-colors: the OS replaces our palette
   and the hues collapse, but icon shape + leading word still carry meaning
   and icons follow system text color; pin links to LinkText. Never set
   forced-color-adjust:none. */
@media (forced-colors: active) {
  .ds-alert a { color: LinkText; }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .ds-alert-dismiss { transition: none; }
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ACCORDION  (.ds-acc / .ds-acc-stack / .ds-acc-body / .ds-acc-rail)
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Native <details>/<summary> disclosure — no JS, keyboard and screen-
   reader semantics for free, and find-in-page can auto-expand panels.
   A +/− glyph replaces the default marker. Two dressings, one element:

     - Card (default): white surface, hairline border, 6px radius —
       stands alone on the page. Stack several in .ds-acc-stack (8px gap).
     - Rail (.ds-acc-rail, added to .ds-acc): card chrome dropped —
       background, border, and radius go; the surrounding rail's hairline
       dividers do the separating. Internals go single-column for the
       narrow rail, and the +/− marker turns Link Blue so closed
       disclosures still read as interactive (Open Blue is too light
       for a glyph).

   Body internals: a <dl> inside .ds-acc-body gets the standard metadata
   layout — condensed-caps <dt> labels beside regular <dd> values
   (two-column in cards, single-column in the rail variant).

   Content rule (organizing-content.html): never put must-see information
   ONLY inside a closed accordion — required warnings also surface in
   always-visible flow. Default state is closed; a single most-relevant
   panel may start open. Open state is not persisted.

   Adds over the mockup source: a :focus-visible ring on the summary, and
   the rail summary grows its hit area to the 24px target-size floor via
   the padding + negative-margin technique (DESIGN-POLICIES.md, Chrome
   and interaction structure) with no layout change. No transitions —
   nothing for prefers-reduced-motion to disable.

   Validated 2026-06-22 → 2026-07-27 as .mg-acc in
   mockups/merged-abstract-reader.html (paper-info card group + abstract
   rail); treatment agreed on design-patterns/organizing-content.html.

   Example:
     <div class="ds-acc-stack">
       <details class="ds-acc" open>
         <summary>Paper information</summary>
         <div class="ds-acc-body">
           <dl>
             <dt>arXiv ID</dt><dd><a href="…">2604.22725</a></dd>
             <dt>License</dt><dd><a href="…">CC BY 4.0</a></dd>
           </dl>
         </div>
       </details>
     </div>
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.ds-acc-stack { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
.ds-acc {
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid var(--arxiv-border-light);
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-family: var(--arxiv-font-sans);
}
.ds-acc > summary {
  cursor: pointer;
  list-style: none;
  font-size: 0.92rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--arxiv-ink);
  padding: 11px 16px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.ds-acc > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.ds-acc > summary::marker { content: ""; }
.ds-acc > summary::after {
  content: "+";
  content: "+" / "";  /* alt-text form: the glyph is decorative to AT —
                         <details> already announces expanded/collapsed */
  margin-left: auto;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--arxiv-grey);
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1;
}
.ds-acc[open] > summary::after { content: "−"; content: "−" / ""; }
.ds-acc[open] > summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--arxiv-border-light); }
.ds-acc > summary:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid var(--arxiv-focus-ring);
  outline-offset: -2px;  /* ring sits inside the card edge */
  border-radius: 6px;
}
.ds-acc-body { padding: 14px 16px 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--arxiv-ink); }
.ds-acc-body dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 7px 18px; margin: 0; }
.ds-acc-body dt { font-family: var(--arxiv-font-condensed); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--arxiv-grey); white-space: nowrap; padding-top: 2px; }

